# Unpublished navigation-only fix after Sites v515

Base source:506c754a5fa0f558638e9098795fa4a474331c61.
Expected contract: in-app accounting card opens report/wizard with a pushed history entry; wizard close only dismisses wizard; Back returns to the actual previous scoped screen. A direct report without usable previous context falls back to Finance for the selected month/venue.

Confirmed defects:
1. Plain card anchor caused a full document navigation; initial navigation seeding could replace the actual warehouse return context with a synthetic parent.
2. Closing wizard only changed React state; closeMonth=1 remained in URL and the navigation contract still treated the report as a wizard. Header fallback was unscoped /finance.
3. On direct loads, bootstrap ran before navigation-contract availability, so synthetic parent could become /home. Actual isolated history.state.bdPreviousUrl=/home reproduced this.

Fixes: plain unmodified card clicks use existing bdNavigate push/popstate mechanism (modified clicks remain native). Wizard close removes only closeMonth through existing replace-query helper. Reports canonical parent includes month/venue; bootstrap constructs Reports parent from current URL independently of script load order. No shared header behavior changes, calculations, APIs, permissions, storage formats or business writes.

